<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Constantine Bodin</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. c. 1101</span> · <a href="/centuries/11th-century">11th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Constantine Bodin was King of Duklja from about 1081 to around 1101, son of Mihailo I. In 1072 Bulgarian rebels proclaimed him tsar as Peter III, but the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/byzantine-empire">Byzantines</a> defeated and captured him. As king he extended his rule over Raška and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bosnia">Bosnia</a> and secured an archbishopric at Bar in 1089. After his death the realm declined in dynastic strife.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/constantine-bodin.jpg" alt="Constantine Bodin" width="320" height="167" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Constantine Bodin · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Seal_of_Constantine_Bodin.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
